VALUES ('VJ-2zqbY33E','Machu Picchu - The secrets of the Inca builders | DW Documentary','The Inca city of Machu Picchu in Peru has been uninhabited for centuries. But it is nevertheless well preserved. Discovered at the beginning of the 20th century, it attracts around 1.5 million visitors from all over the world every year. At an altitude of more than 2,400 meters, the Incas succeeded in building a masterpiece of architecture and engineering. Located on a mountain ridge in the Andes, it is a place in perfect harmony with nature. The several dozen buildings of Machu Picchu cover 10 hectares. Their interlocking stone construction has withstood centuries of heavy rainfall and frequent landslides. The Incas built the city in the 15th century. They did not have a writing system in the conventional modern sense. Instead, they developed a unique recording system consisting of knotted strings, known as "quipus." With their advanced technical skills, they succeeded in building complex drainage systems and designing buildings based on a map of the heavens. Thanks to the research and findings of experts and spectacular 3D animations, some of the secrets behind the construction of Machu Picchu can now be revealed, allowing us to discover the genius of the Inca builders. #documentary #dwdocumentary #dwdocs #machupicchu ______ DW Documentary gives you knowledge beyond the headlines. Watch top documentaries from German broadcasters and international production companies. Meet intriguing people, travel to distant lands, get a look behind the complexities of daily life and build a deeper understanding of current affairs and global events. Subscribe and explore the world around you with DW Documentary. Subscribe to: ‬ ⮞ DW Documentary (English): https://www.youtube.com/@DWDocumentary ⮞ DW Documental (Spanish): https://www.youtube.com/@DWDocumental ⮞ DW Documentary وثائقية دي دبليو (Arabic): https://www.youtube.com/@dwdocarabia ⮞ DW Documentary हिन्दी (Hindi): https://www.youtube.co